      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOLDEN SUNSET (1) made an impressive return when coming from a 30m handicap to get home narrowly here last week. Should enjoy a cosy run from the ace draw and with added fitness under the belt can make it two on the bounce. PINNIE (2) was fourth behind GOLDEN SUNSET as favourite last week but won two in a row prior, coming from wider to cruise home here prior. Draws well so worth another chance. KEAYANG STUKA (5) has joined Shane Graham since last seen finishing midfield in the Inter Dominion Final. Accomplished pacer who generally comes to hand very quickly, with four wins from five first-up appearances. Draws widest but has trialled and won his lone try at this distance. SHEZA CHANCE (4) steps up in grade but deserves some respect off back-to-back wins.",
